Modification (the only changes from upstream 18.1.3):
1. src/Lexer.ts: a fast path in the inline lexer (#tokenizeInlines) plus a
   findPlainChunkEnd helper. A run of plain inline text — no character that can
   start a non-text inline token (backslash, <, [, !, backtick, *, _, ~, &, @,
   www., ://, mailto:, xmpp:, or a hard break), with email-aware handling so
   an address containing `_` is still autolinked whole — is emitted directly
   as the single text token marked's inline lexer would produce, without
   running the tokenizers or the inline text regex. Every other run goes
   through marked's inline lexer unchanged. A run holding `@` takes no fast
   path at all: the email lookahead in the text rule can advance the loop one
   character at a time toward a `www.` the URL tokenizer then autolinks even
   mid-word, so a plain-text chunk in such a run is not provably plain.
2. src/Tokenizer.ts: the list tokenizer takes a line with indexOf + slice
   (takeFirstLine) instead of split('\n', 1)[0], avoiding an array allocation
   per line; and its inner loop skips the six block-start regex tests for a
   line whose first non-space character (within the item indent) cannot start
   any of them (fence, heading, html, blockquote, bullet, hr) — a plain
   continuation line, the common case.
The changes are pure speedups: they cannot alter any output.
